 "blueprint_update": {
  "snapshot": "main-20261015",
  "statement": "Let $\\varphi\\colon A\\to B$ be a ring map, let $I\\subseteq A$ be an ideal,\nput $J=IB$, and let $a\\in I$ with image $b=\\varphi(a)$. Then the chart ring\n$B[J/b]$ of the blow-up of $J$ is generated as a ring by the images of $B$\nand of the chart ring $A[I/a]$. Equivalently, the homomorphism\n$\\sigma_a\\colon B\\otimes_AA[I/a]\\to B[J/b]$ is surjective.",
  "proof": [
   {
    "text": "By [lemma-nagata-chart-ring-normal-form], the target is generated as a\n$B$-algebra by the fractions $z/b$ with $z\\in J$. Write\n$z=\\sum_k y_k\\overline{x_k}$ with $x_k\\in I$. Then\n\n$$\nz/b=\\sum_k\\sigma_a\\bigl(y_k\\otimes(x_k/a)\\bigr),\n$$\n\nproving surjectivity.",
    "uses": [
     "lemma-nagata-chart-ring-normal-form"
    ],
    "elementary": false
   }
  ],
